---
// VISUAILS — upload guidelines. Ported from the SvelteKit
// upload-guidelines page (itself ported from static /upload-guidelines.html).
// The source used the ProductScene placeholder for its two example
// scenes rather than a real photo (there's no real "bad vs. good" photo
// pair for this exact moment in IMAGES.md), so that’s kept as-is here.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { TEST_SAMPLE } from '../data/pricing.js';

// The test-sample fee was typed here too. It is a tier fact, so it comes from
// pricing.js — see src/pages/test-sample.astro for the same correction.
const SAMPLE = TEST_SAMPLE.en;
/* ── DE ONDERGRENS STAAT NU OP DE PAGINA DIE HEM VRAAGT — 23 augustus 2026 ──
 *
 * Hier stond "Send the highest resolution you have" en verder niets over
 * formaat. Sinds vandaag WEIGERT het bestelformulier een foto onder een
 * ondergrens (zie keurBeeld() in src/data/shots.js), en een weigering die
 * nergens is aangekondigd, is een weigering die iemand op stap 2 tegenkomt
 * zonder te weten wat hij dan moet.
 *
 * Uit de constante en niet ingetypt, om dezelfde reden als de bewaartermijnen in
 * terms.astro: dit is een getal dat de code afdwingt, en een pagina die er zijn
 * eigen versie van bijhoudt, belooft op een dag iets anders dan er gebeurt. */
import { MIN_LANGE_ZIJDE } from '../data/shots.js';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import ProductScene from '../components/ProductScene.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Upload guidelines — VISUAILS"
  description="Simple tips for the product photos you send us, so your visuals come out sharp, accurate and fast."
>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow-page">Getting the best results</span>
    <h1 class="display">How to photograph your product so we can match it exactly</h1>
    <p class="lead" style="margin-top:1.1rem">You don’t need a studio — just a clear photo and a few simple habits.</p>
    {/* /guides had no inbound link from anywhere in the body of the site
        (brief §1 wires it into the chain), and this is the page it points at
        first. The link goes in the lead rather than a related-pages block:
        someone reading a guide is exactly who wants the rest of them. */}
    <p class="hub-note">Of everything in the <a href="/guides/">guides</a>, this is the one to read before you order — every step after it works better when the photo going in is right.</p>
    <div class="flex" style="margin-top:1.8rem">
      <a href="/test-sample/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">{SAMPLE.cta}</a>
      <a href="/start/" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Start an order</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="container">
    <div class="grid grid-2 reveal-group">
      <div class="card reveal pending">
        <h2 class="as-h3" style="color:var(--ink)">Do</h2>
        <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span>Keep it clear &amp; sharp — in focus, no motion blur.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span>Use a neutral, uncluttered background.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span>Light it well and evenly — daylight works great.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span>Show the full product, plus a few close-ups of key details.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" /></svg><span>Send the highest resolution you have — at least {MIN_LANGE_ZIJDE} pixels on the long side, which any phone from the last decade clears. Below that the upload is refused on the spot and says so, so you find out while you are still at your desk rather than a day later.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      {/* This card used to carry a bespoke red — oklch(0.78 0.15 25) on the
          heading and every icon. Three things were wrong with it at once. It
          was outside sRGB by 0.096, so the browser gamut-mapped it and the
          colour that shipped was never the one authored. At 2.02:1 on paper it
          failed WCAG on an h3 outright. And it was the only saturated colour
          on any marketing page, against global.css's own fence: system colour
          never appears here, marketing is ink, paper and photography.

          The replacement says "lesser" the way this page already says it forty
          lines down, where .not-ideal desaturates and dims the weaker
          ProductScene rather than labelling it red: recess the ground. The ✕
          against the ✓ and the heading carry the meaning; they always did. */}
      <div class="card reveal pending" style="background:var(--surface-2)">
        <h2 class="as-h3" style="color:var(--ink)">Avoid</h2>
        <ul class="checklist" style="margin-top:1rem">
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg><span>Blurry, dark or low-light shots.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg><span>Busy or distracting backgrounds.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg><span>Heavy filters or strong colour casts.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg><span>Tiny, low-res screenshots.</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="i" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6L6 18M6 6l12 12" /></svg><span>Cropping part of the product out of frame.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    {/* ── TWEE ECHTE FOTO'S, GEEN TEKENING — 20 augustus 2026 ─────────────────
        Hier stonden twee `<ProductScene>`-illustraties: dezelfde getekende fles,
        één met het label "niet ideaal" en één met "goed". Dat is een tekening die
        beweert iets over fotografie te laten zien, en dat kan een tekening niet.
        Deze pagina is de enige op de site die de bezoeker vraagt zélf een foto te
        maken; hij moet het verschil kunnen ZIEN, niet lezen dat er verschil is.

        Placeholders in plaats van niets, zodat `npm run placeholders` deze twee
        blijft tellen tot ze er zijn — zie de noot in Placeholder.astro. De
        opdracht staat eronder: het moet hetzelfde product zijn in allebei de
        kaders, want anders vergelijk je twee producten in plaats van twee foto's. */}
    <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <div class="reveal pending not-ideal">
        <Placeholder
          lang="en"
          ratio="4 / 3"
          subject={`The same product shot badly: a phone photo in a dim room, on a cluttered surface, slightly out of focus`}
          message={`Must look like a photo someone would actually send us — not a caricature. Dim, flat, a busy background, and just soft enough that the edge of the product is not crisp. Same product and same angle as the frame beside it; only the conditions differ.`}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="reveal pending">
        <Placeholder
          lang="en"
          ratio="4 / 3"
          subject={`The same product shot well: daylight from a window, a plain surface, sharp from edge to edge`}
          message={`Must be reachable with a phone and no equipment — that is the whole promise of this page. Daylight, a plain wall or table, product filling the frame, in focus. Nothing styled, nothing retouched; if it looks like studio work the reader concludes they cannot do it.`}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>The set we recommend — <em>and why.</em></h2>
        <p>We almost never hold your product in our hands, so the more angles you send, the more exactly we can rebuild it. That is what makes the difference between matching your product and approximating it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="req-grid reveal-group">
        <div class="req-card reveal pending"><span class="rc-num">01</span><h3>Front &amp; back</h3><p>The whole product from both sides, so nothing about its shape is guessed.</p></div>
        <div class="req-card reveal pending"><span class="rc-num">02</span><h3>A detail close-up</h3><p>Logos, stitching, prints, hardware — the things that have to stay exact.</p></div>
        <div class="req-card reveal pending"><span class="rc-num">03</span><h3>The fabric</h3><p>A close shot of the material so texture, weave and sheen read true.</p></div>
        <div class="req-card reveal pending"><span class="rc-num">04</span><h3>Worn for fit</h3><p>Someone actually wearing it, so we can reproduce the real-world fit and drape.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="req-note reveal pending"><strong>The first one is required. The rest are recommended.</strong> Front and back both come back to you as delivered images, so we ask for both rather than invent the side we cannot see. The close-up and the worn shot are optional — each one makes a specific thing more accurate, and if a product has no logo or hardware to close in on, the close-up you get back is a fabric shot instead.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band reveal pending">
    <h2 class="display" style="font-size:var(--t-page-h1-sm)">Got a photo ready? Let’s see it transformed.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin:1rem auto 0;text-align:center">Start with one test sample — just a {SAMPLE.feeNote}.</p>
    <div class="flex" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:1.8rem">
      <a href="/test-sample/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Test sample</a>
      <a href="/start/" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Start an order</a>
    </div>
  </div></div></section>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Desaturated treatment for the "not ideal" example — mirrors the static
     site's .ba-before-scene filter, scoped here since it’s only used once. */
  /* HET FILTER OP HET ZWAKKE KADER IS WEG — 20 augustus 2026.
     `.not-ideal` stond op `saturate(.4) brightness(.92) contrast(.92)`, en dat
     klopte zolang er een TEKENING in stond: een illustratie die niemand voor een
     foto aanziet, mag je dempen om te laten zien welke kant je op moet kijken.
     Er komt nu een echte foto in van hoe een slechte inzending eruitziet, en die
     mag je niet nabewerken — dan zegt het beeld niet meer "zo ziet een slechte
     foto eruit" maar "wij hebben deze foto slechter gemaakt". Het kruisje, de
     kop en de opdracht eronder dragen de betekenis; die deden dat altijd al. */

  /* The line back to the guides hub. Body copy under the lead, not a badge. */
  .hub-note { margin-top: .9rem; max-width: 62ch; font-size: .92rem; color: var(--ink-3); line-height: 1.6; }
  .hub-note a { color: var(--accent-bright); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
